diff --git a/features/todo-filtering.feature b/features/todo-filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a1148a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+Feature: Todo Filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I can focus on specific items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded with a fresh todo list
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+
+  Scenario: The All route shows all todos
+    Given the user is on the "#/" route
+    When the page loads
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: The Active route shows only active todos
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the "All" filter link does not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: The Completed route shows only completed todos
+    When the user clicks the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item with title "Walk dog"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Item updated while filtered is hidden correctly
+    Given the user is on the Active filter
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list is empty
+    And "Buy milk" is no longer visible in the filtered view
+
+  Scenario: Switching back to All from a filtered view restores all items
+    Given the user is on the Active filter
+    When the user clicks the "All" filter
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: The default route is All
+    Given the page URL has no hash fragment
+    When the page loads
+    Then the "All" filter link has class "selected"
diff --git a/features/todo-management.feature b/features/todo-management.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9692245
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-management.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+Feature: Todo Management
+  As a user
+  I want to add, complete, edit, and remove todo items
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded with a fresh todo list
+
+  Scenario: Adding a new todo appends it to the list and clears the input
+    Given the new-todo input contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Empty input is ignored when adding a todo
+    Given the new-todo input contains "   "
+    When the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo toggles its completed state
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" item has class "completed"
+    And the "Buy milk" toggle checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" item has class "editing"
+    And the edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on Enter updates the todo title
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user is editing "Buy milk"
+    When the user types "Buy organic milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy organic milk"
+    And the "Buy organic milk" item does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur updates the todo title
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user is editing "Buy milk"
+    When the user types "Buy organic milk" and the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy organic milk"
+    And the "Buy organic milk" item does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user is editing "Buy milk"
+    When the user clears the input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape during editing discards the changes
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user is editing "Buy milk" to "Buy organic milk"
+    When the user presses Escape
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    And the "Buy milk" item does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo removes it
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all marks every todo as complete
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todo items have class "completed"
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes only the completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Walk dog"
+    And the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: The todo count shows the number of active items with pluralized text
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" and "Feed cat"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    Then the todo-count shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: The todo count shows singular text for 1 active item
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    Then the main section is not visible
+    And the footer section is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are shown when there are todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer section is visible
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1e8c3d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Todo Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved in localStorage
+  So that they persist across page reloads
+
+  Background:
+    Given the page is loaded with a fresh todo list
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage with the correct key and format
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the title of item 1 is "Buy milk"
+    And item 1 is not completed
+    And the title of item 2 is "Walk dog"
+    And item 2 is completed
+    And the localStorage key is "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    And the user is editing "Buy milk" to "Buy organic milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item with title "Buy milk"
+    And the "Buy milk" item does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted across reloads
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Empty state is persisted correctly
+    Given the todo list is empty
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list is empty
+    And the main section is not visible
+    And the footer section is not visible
